56130--db1dcb8d550c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-potter-films-turns-25-ahead-of-new-tv-series-release/a-79856130?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 2001, "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone" hit cinemas and took the world by storm. Today, anticipation for the new series is high, but its creator, J.K. Rowling, remains a controversial figure.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dffa41f33ac437ea376df228b4b05c933b762c2d39dbca839dc90c263589fc90</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>BMW reports lower Q3 earnings as China woes mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f6b8c29821560a5cc18a83f5720ce8a6c85e43d0bcf91ad68c06ab5e218e989</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847--9f74c40c2952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">BMW reports a drop in profits in the July to September quarter amid fierce competition from China.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's celebrated children's author Janosch has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d55e89a31a4a56d05d863e67b285e5da64fbcf496c7d4da16d47285c4c517e1d</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600--a3fdc8a2501b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bear, Tiger and Tiger-Duck: The author and illustrator Janosch achieved world fame with his heartwarming children's figures. He died at the age of 95.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>From rotten food to political opponents: Researchers explore how disgust relates to our beliefs, and why the connection is complicated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7790a680108b0d8bae4d64df2b01b7e2c4dd02587b2c8bad71c81b05358e696a</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T05:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-w/a-79734659--e9b7cd7e436d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-why-the-connection-is-complicated/a-79734659?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some studies have linked disgust sensitivity to socially conservative attitudes. But does disgust shape our politics, or do our beliefs shape what we find disgusting?</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How Berlin's Arab queers are building their community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daa5cdf2ddf712739e56c632e74e95f13bf464ccbec397607f43d70e1c43f3be</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143--c676c7f349f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the co-founder of the ADIRA Drag Festival, Lebanese performance artist, drag performer, DJ and cultural organizer Hassandra has become an essential part of Berlin's queer artistic landscape.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Cyprus: From ties with Russia to a strategic alignment with the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89e98e75702d7f32bf926ae7941026510d70b4a9d61d82b8e696fec32283fe55</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251--5a66c266e064.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Republic of Cyprus long balanced ties between Russia and the West. Now, it is phasing out Russian weapons, expanding defense cooperation with the United States and redefining its place in the Eastern Mediterranean.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Multiple flights to European airports targeted by bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75534ff823a02615d28667db9d3424596d817eeb939aa5118f644f6f32250399</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434--863c4364baea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bomb threats involved two passenger planes bound for Warsaw, a Ryanair flight from London to Spain, two flights to Rome and a flight traveling from Israel to the Bulgarian capital, Sofia. No explosives were found.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Football: Spanish player dies on after cardiac arrest on the pitch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7810cd75cc9dee182ce01415fecbf9159d11af6a6f3dc3260dac6f7bb24d738a</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-spanish-player-dies-on-after-cardiac-arrest-on-the-pitch/a-79839398--59e3eb0d85d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-spanish-player-dies-on-after-cardiac-arrest-on-the-pitch/a-79839398?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tenerife forward Jesus de Miguel has died following a collision with the opposing goalkeeper. The Spanish second-division club has said it is "heartbroken" by the loss.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Asian Cup postponed due to Middle East conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34a75cb6f03fbf30656cee190c66f345cddc2857d35621f753a9633101f07ba4</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/asian-cup-postponed-due-to-middle-east-conflict/a-79837334--1d2a8af2e01e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/asian-cup-postponed-due-to-middle-east-conflict/a-79837334?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Cup has become the latest sporting event to be affected by the ongoing conflict in the Middle East. Organizers cite "exceptional circumstances" in Saudi Arabia, which has seen several Houthi attacks of late.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Could the AI boom make borrowing more expensive in Europe?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:272659484da9447b5687ee31ff4e8925ac735cca1939ee2cab58cac27eb71c4b</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T10:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-the-ai-boom-make-borrowing-more-expensive-in-europe/a-79511985--c654959bd451.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-the-ai-boom-make-borrowing-more-expensive-in-europe/a-79511985?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France, Germany and Italy face a volatile bond market as war inflation bites. With US tech giants now issuing billions in AI bonds, they are competing with cash-strapped European governments.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Ukraine in focus at Berlin Security Conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:085e43614130460e6987264ff35fe2c188aa6bcf780faa44a16df3162e4782d0</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T07:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ukraine-in-focus-at-berlin-security-conference/live-79835322--417ad1cade50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ukraine-in-focus-at-berlin-security-conference/live-79835322?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A security conference in the German capital is addressing defending Europe against threats from Russia. Meanwhile, Germany's justice minister wants to raise penalties for sexual offenses. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey officials considering options after CAS order to reinstate Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0b40eae1988759714be739240cd55bed36112bb3d38af2e6ca0e59b3431a9a8</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451--d3d6cb0a329c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's ruling body is deciding how to respond to a decision by the Court of Arbitration for Sport that allows Russia back into international competition. Germany hasn't ruled out pulling out as a tournament host.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>LA communities kick out Big Oil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc504c6dd119218ece23fb018cf5c9c4196334d866f714dd8a14d9112d964281</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843--72df9d2c6283.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of advocacy from residents and legal battles with Big Oil, Los Angeles voted to ban drilling and phase out oil extraction in the city. It's the first city in the United States to kick the oil industry out.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Global pedestrian Karl Bushby returns home to UK after 28-year trek</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c234db74eacff502ab7d35fc6163ea3f7cf3181f5dcb59f6e9340f74eae3a4c5</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-pedestrian-karl-bushby-returns-home-to-uk-after-28-year-trek/a-79829564--7ba09cf0439f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-pedestrian-karl-bushby-returns-home-to-uk-after-28-year-trek/a-79829564?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Karl Bushby, a British man who traveled 50,000 km without transport over the past 28 years, has come home. Starting in Chile, he crossed the Americas, Russia and parts of Central Asia and Europe — almost all on foot.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Iliana Yotova won the presidential election in Bulgaria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3aeb7466d6d5439523b5bf1ebdf67ef8d6a44df2ec0d3884a9ee175c4f8fdeb</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-iliana-yotova-won-the-presidential-election-in-bulgaria/a-79829019--beeabc4abe9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-iliana-yotova-won-the-presidential-election-in-bulgaria/a-79829019?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iliana Yotova won the presidential election in Bulgaria, promising to be a "president of peace." But the campaign showed how divided Bulgarians are about the war in Ukraine and drone attacks in the Black Sea.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Merz says next German president 'must be a woman' — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba485ca3a53aa73bd18d6f1d6e0c8e7818d95332c0ce31cdd930561616e3317d</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T07:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-says-next-german-president-must-be-a-woman-report/live-79825749--f592c9770ada.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-says-next-german-president-must-be-a-woman-report/live-79825749?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German President Frank-Walter Steinmeier's second term is due to end in March next year. Meanwhile, Merz has called for 'digital sovereignty' in the era of AI.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Kimi Antonelli makes history as youngest F1 champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c77a05dcf28b24f74d6490c2972eb8608a32b5968ce91d813b79fad5b6c86e96</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T05:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kimi-antonelli-makes-history-as-youngest-f1-champion/a-79825130--6d0086c2458b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kimi-antonelli-makes-history-as-youngest-f1-champion/a-79825130?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kimi Antonelli became Formula One's youngest world champion and Italy's first since 1953 when he finished third in Sunday's thrilling and crash-hit Mexico City Grand Prix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's giant new radar in Kaliningrad raises alarm in NATO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:564ca2a87240915264be90bf1bad0b995ed957ff862b7e4c1c352b9dfd8486ce</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T20:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815--4cdeadba9801.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia is nearing completion of what experts think is a giant radar complex in Kaliningrad, capable of monitoring much of Europe. Experts warn the project could intensify the military standoff between Moscow and NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethnic Germans in Kazakhstan face legacy of the Soviet Union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79241903d448e557b33d31b6e0aceb507147bdc5f76701c4459b3e3e5ffdeb49</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethnic-germans-in-kazakhstan-face-legacy-of-the-soviet-union/a-79754048--09fc50df10b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethnic-germans-in-kazakhstan-face-legacy-of-the-soviet-union/a-79754048?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kazakhstan is struggling to deal with the legacy of the Soviet dictatorship. Some 85 years ago, Stalin deported hundreds of thousands of people: Some 400,000 ethnic Germans living in the USSR were sent to Kazakhstan.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's search for a nuclear waste site</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf1ad06af7d08590a895708540d9f96991c3adc2fb3403fb3318d24cb1c9608e</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T08:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-search-for-a-nuclear-waste-site/a-79820678--66cee2f12295.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-search-for-a-nuclear-waste-site/a-79820678?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finland has become the first country with a final storage facility for nuclear waste. Germany is still searching for a site, while some countries have yet to start. Costs are expected to total many billions of euros.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia after Vucic: The winners are losing patience</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d0a7bade82ed7a43625f3ce3ad326e5acb7d3bdb82298322282c2b699780380</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T19:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586--7cebe42bf331.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After the Student List's election victory, Aleksandar Vucic's power apparatus is disintegrating. People want justice as soon as possible. But the losers still hold sway in the judiciary and administration.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Gen Z protests disrupted by violence on Saturday</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2a13d87f4674e6fe27af3010d2317e001ae65b22e454f29001a896f23c9b7c1</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-disrupted-by-violence-on-saturday/live-79814694--76fbedb708ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-disrupted-by-violence-on-saturday/live-79814694?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nationwide protests led by young people were largely peaceful throughout the day, but reports about looting and rioting in the evening, especially in Frankfurt, overshadowed the spirit of the demonstrations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Embarrassing name? How we live with names we don't like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be226fd4a0dd8c84970c1cd80d848cadabb8617d5dd3cc68629de4de711a37b4</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T05:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/embarrassing-name-how-we-live-with-names-we-don-t-like/a-79724068--afb6ee0b7720.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/embarrassing-name-how-we-live-with-names-we-don-t-like/a-79724068?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">What happens when your name evokes laughter or ridicule? Research points to negative life outcomes, but some people learn to embrace unfortunate names.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Canadian PM Mark Carney discusses talks with the EU, overdependence on the US and how to deal with Donald Trump in a DW interview.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fe62dbaef40b7a0257fdd5468a610bb3d64cbb7c90ebbb6e98c6437f375b072</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T20:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-do/a-79811469--a55bfac7d94c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-donald-trump-in-a-dw-interview/a-79811469?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Mark Carney tells DW that Canada is seeking closer EU ties to "diversify and deepen" partnerships beyond the Americas. Despite German pushback, he said he favors the all-new term "associate membership."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What the rift within the Tsikhanouski family means for the Belarusian opposition in exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e0008768f0b700a01fe4f4402d6c6addaaab4fef3eaa142f1c565fcfaafc95d</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776--7fdd2527b18a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Siarhei Tsikhanouski criticizes the work of his wife, Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya, and her office. He also questions her legitimacy. What are the implications for Belarusian political forces in exile?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz hopes for Korean reunification at DMZ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1657f82eb8166ac50f7a5c00a85517f6aec531b7520465d7be676377335ac0da</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-hopes-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462--f2cebaec800e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-hopes-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has expressed hope for Korean reunification during a visit to the heavily fortified border. Meanwhile, President Steinmeier has held talks with China's Xi Jinping in Beijing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Kenya friendly highlights Africa's growing pull for global sport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b9f2393f67f1d880b27571f1960feda024f7eb6869147151e69e7620017d3a1</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753--c6f4b50cf1c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich are to open Nairobi's new Raila Odinga International Stadium against Ajax as Kenya prepares for AFCON 2027. The match highlights Africa's growing sports ambitions — and questions over cost and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany takes cautious approach on Israeli election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba0ed2294eb50102031aced8ae3f04bac8c055e3687af17d5dab9c3c848a36f2</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184--6eb977f23eb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German politicians have been slow to respond as they wait to see who is likely to comprise the next coalition. Many are also hoping for a government without religious hardliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>IIHF ordered to allow Russia back into world championships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c27da3d767d3bb53ccda87a5edc96d10e73aa2746622ae784d04f330095a0bac</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650--8e19bd1daa6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has ruled that Russian teams must be allowed to take part in international ice hockey tournaments. The IIHF had banned Russia following the country's full-scale invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Many Turkish 'guest workers' hit by poverty in old age</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b11531481bd091c83138884259d30078a52007e9de336a22ac3a1ede62e532e1</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/many-turkish-guest-workers-hit-by-poverty-in-old-age/a-79746838--0d5019a9af26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/many-turkish-guest-workers-hit-by-poverty-in-old-age/a-79746838?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">West Germany and Turkey signed an agreement allowing the temporary recruitment of workers on October 30, 1961. Sixty-five years on, many so-called 'guest workers' can't live from their pensions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The dachshund, a humorous icon with political symbolism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13b937bb4a2d4f2d263aeff82269d103c2dba26f2bf78ddda41e2a8fd58b6e80</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../.